title: PT_D1_Start
---
// ================================================================
// PLAYTEST_Demo.yarn — a two-day mini demo that is also the play test
// of one full game loop, and the reference for writing a new day.
//
// Run: on [GameLoop] › FlowWiring set Day Schedule to DaySchedule_PlayTest
//      (Assets/[02]Script/Day Schedule/), then Play. Set it back to
//      DaySchedule_Demo afterwards.
//
// Every command and function in Docs/YarnCommands/ is used once at least,
// except save_chapter_node (see PT_D2_Close). Lines starting with (PT)
// print what the game state should be; delete them in a real day.
// (Not "[PT]": Yarn reads square brackets as markup and the speaker name breaks.)
//
// The shape of a day (copy this when writing a new one):
//   BeforeOpen  › Story  : the day's start node, set in the Day Schedule
//                          (Day / Start Node / Chapter Name). Pre-opening story.
//                          <<flow_check_events>> shows the day's popups mid-story.
//                          <<flow_open_bar>> ends it (required, or the day hangs here).
//   Open        › Talking: customers walk in, talk, order. Chapter title fades in.
//                          <<flow_prepare_drinks>> + <<wait_for_task>> = the player
//                          makes the drink; the story waits until it is served.
//   Close                : <<flow_close_bar>> from Talking.
//   next day             : <<flow_next_day>> from Close adds 1 to $day. The next
//                          day's start node begins when THIS dialogue ends, so
//                          make flow_next_day the last thing in the day.
// ================================================================

// A new day starts with a clean Event Log.
<<eventlog_clear>>

// The bar is locked and the camera fixed until the customer orders.
<<Enable_InteractableObject SystemGame false>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Cut_Camera CamController MainCam>>

Player: (PT) Day {$day}. flow_phase = {flow_phase()}, flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect 1 / BeforeOpen / StoryBeforeOpen)
Player: First night of the play test.
Player: Let me check the notice board before I open.

// Back to Event: shows any queued popups and waits until the player closes them,
// then the next line plays. Nothing queues popups yet, so it passes at once.
<<flow_check_events>>
Player: (PT) After flow_check_events: flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect StoryBeforeOpen)

Player: Nothing new. Time to open.
<<wait_scene 1>>

// Leaves BeforeOpen for Open › Talking. The Chapter Name of today's row fades in.
<<flow_open_bar>>
Player: (PT) flow_phase = {flow_phase()}, flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect Open / TalkingWithCustomer)
<<jump PT_D1_Isla>>
===

title: PT_D1_Isla
---
// ── A customer walks in ─────────────────────────────
<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Isla 2>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController CenterCam>>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
Isla: [wave]Evening! Is this place open yet?[/wave]
Player: Just opened. Take a seat.
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Left>>
Isla: Cosy. I like it.
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Forward>>

// ── The order: a drink by name ──────────────────────
// order_customer names who the next order is for (it scores their preferences).
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Isla>>
Isla: I'll have a [order]{Order_Cocktail_ByName_OutName("Gin Fizz")}[/order], please.
Player: {Order_Cocktail_ByName_OutDescription("Gin Fizz")}
Player: (PT) order_name = {order_name()}, order_type = {order_type()}, order_flavor = {order_flavor()}

<<jump PT_MakeDrink>>
===

title: PT_MakeDrink
---
// Shared by every order in this file. The player normally makes the drink;
// the second option walks every step from Yarn instead (no ingredients, so it
// scores Fail) to show the step commands and to speed up a test run.

// Pre-selects the minigame of the next step 2.2. The player's Shake/Stir button overrides it.
<<flow_minigame Shaking>>
Player: (PT) flow_minigame_type = {flow_minigame_type()} (expect Shaking)

-> Make the drink
    <<flow_prepare_drinks>>
    <<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
-> (Test) Let Yarn walk the steps
    <<flow_prepare_drinks>>
    Player: (PT) step = {flow_step()} (expect AddIngredient)
    <<flow_ingredient_added>>
    Player: (PT) flow_ingredient_added: step = {flow_step()} (expect Minigame)
    <<flow_another_ingredient>>
    Player: (PT) flow_another_ingredient: step = {flow_step()} (expect AddIngredient)
    <<flow_ingredient_added Stirring>>
    <<flow_drink_complete>>
    Player: (PT) flow_drink_complete: step = {flow_step()} (expect Garnish)
    <<flow_remake_drink>>
    Player: (PT) flow_remake_drink: step = {flow_step()} (expect AddIngredient, nothing scored)
    <<flow_ingredient_added>>
    <<flow_drink_complete>>
    <<flow_garnish_done>>
    Player: (PT) flow_garnish_done: step = {flow_step()} (expect Serve)
    <<flow_serve_done>>
    Player: (PT) flow_serve_done: step = {flow_step()} (expect TalkingWithCustomer, scored here)

// Waits until the drink is served and scored, then writes $satisfaction and
// $type_of_cocktail. After the test option it returns at once.
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>

<<Enable_InteractableObject SystemGame false>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
Player: (PT) order_satisfaction = {order_satisfaction()}, served type = {$type_of_cocktail}, minigame result = "{flow_minigame_result()}"

<<if $day == 1>>
    <<jump PT_D1_Reaction>>
<<else>>
    <<jump PT_D2_Reaction>>
<<endif>>
===

title: PT_D1_Reaction
---
// ── React to the drink ($satisfaction is set by wait_for_task) ──
<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
    Isla: [bounce]Perfect. Just how I like it.[/bounce]
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    Isla: Not bad. A little different, but fine.
<<else>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "upset">>
    Isla: [shake]Hmm... that's not what I asked for.[/shake]
<<endif>>

// Clears the order and the three result variables for the next customer.
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
Isla: See you tomorrow.
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Isla>>
<<jump PT_D1_Close>>
===

title: PT_D1_Close
---
// ── End of day 1 ────────────────────────────────────
Player: That's it for tonight.
<<flow_close_bar>>
Player: (PT) flow_phase = {flow_phase()} (expect Close)

<<Panel_FadeOut Panel_Transition>>
// Close -> BeforeOpen: $day becomes 2 and day 2's start node waits for this dialogue to end.
<<flow_next_day>>
<<Panel_FadeIn Panel_Transition>>
// End of node = end of day 1. PT_D2_Start begins next.
===

title: PT_D2_Start
---
<<eventlog_clear>>
<<Enable_InteractableObject SystemGame false>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController MainCam>>

Player: (PT) Day {$day}. flow_phase = {flow_phase()}, flow_step = {flow_step()} (expect 2 / BeforeOpen / StoryBeforeOpen)
Player: Second night. Word must be getting around.
<<flow_open_bar>>
<<jump PT_D2_Walter>>
===

title: PT_D2_Walter
---
<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Walter 1>>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
Walter: Evening, son. Surprise me. Something I'd like.

// ── The order: random from the customer's preferences ─
// The argument is NPC_Name as a number: Cole 1, Owen 2, Walter 3, Freya 4, Isla 5.
// OutName and OutDescription of the same call return the same drink.
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Walter>>
Player: How about a [order]{Order_Cocktail_OutName(3)}[/order]?
Player: {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(3)}
Walter: Go on then.
<<jump PT_MakeDrink>>
===

title: PT_D2_Reaction
---
<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "upset">>
    Walter: [shake]Not my sort of thing.[/shake]
<<else>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: [wiggle]You've got a knack for this.[/wiggle]
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
<<jump PT_D2_Owen>>
===

title: PT_D2_Owen
---
<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Owen 3>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController NearRightCam>>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
Owen: [bounce]Hey hey! Something strong, I don't care what.[/bounce]

// ── The order: a type only ───────────────────────────
// Any drink of that type counts. Instance command: the GameObject name must be
// "[CocktailSystem]" (the object it lives on in the scene). order_name() stays empty.
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Owen>>
<<order_by_type "[CocktailSystem]" HighAlcohol>>
Player: (PT) order_type = {order_type()} (expect HighAlcohol), order_name = "{order_name()}" (expect empty)
Player: One strong drink coming up.

<<flow_prepare_drinks>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>
<<Enable_InteractableObject SystemGame false>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Reset_Camera CamController>>

<<if $type_of_cocktail == TypeOfCocktail.HighAlcohol>>
    Owen: [bounce]Now THAT's strong![/bounce]
<<else>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "upset">>
    Owen: That's... juice, buddy.
<<endif>>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Owen>>
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Walter>>
<<jump PT_D2_Close>>
===

title: PT_D2_Close
---
// ── End of the demo ─────────────────────────────────
// save_chapter_node is left out: [SaveLoadSystem] is inactive in the main scene and the
// dialogue would hang (Docs/YarnCommands/save_chapter_node.md). Save/Load is parked.
Player: Last call. That's the end of the play test.

// Shows the End Shift button (and locks the bar).
<<Can_End_Shift SystemGame>>
<<flow_close_bar>>
<<Fade_To_Summmary Panel_Transition>>
<<Panel_FadeIn Panel_Transition>>
<<DisplayThx>>
Player: (PT) End. flow_phase = {flow_phase()} (expect Close). Thank-you panel should be on screen.
===
